  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Fence refund execution: a locked, committed `processing` row never grants a second provider POST permit, including concurrent and late retries.\n- Hold uncertain outcomes and historical `failed` rows at checkout and line level; no cancellation/re-execution until evidence-backed reconciliation. Preserve provider references and historical status.\n- Use unbounded integer balance comparisons; preserve Int64 API/database amounts.\n- Align merch admin controls and English/Spanish copy with held refunds. An execution-disabled flag is not proof that no money moved.\n- Add source-backed ADR, threat/state model, rollout/rollback guidance and exact red/green test evidence.\n\n## Dependency / review order\n\nDraft, dependent on #393 (`codex/payment-worker-log-safety-20260915`), after the existing payment stack. Do not merge or activate out of order.\n\nThe newer #331 commit `79715507b5ddf6368145ff6f75244c5f0398a472` and mobile diegueins680/tdf-mobile#83 were reviewed but are **not integrated in this branch**. Integrate their contact/qualification/environment-contract changes with the later API/mobile stack in a separate follow-up; do not replace mobile #82 and drop later contracts.\n\n## Verification\n\nBackend source: `5b80af6b4d3ba1367f49d7d464f720bc19d278fb`; final UI source: `28f0652a503dcc6e2c602633e2f3b8f327e6ee01` (backend unchanged).\n\n- Red evidence: PostgreSQL 223 examples/six failures (eight concurrent approvals yielded eight permits); money three examples/two failures, including a QuickCheck overflow counterexample; admin nine tests/four failures.\n- Green: 227 real local PostgreSQL cases; three money cases/100 whole-range QuickCheck inputs; 2,630 complete backend examples; nine targeted mocked admin DOM/accessibility tests; 232 repository tests. All zero failures.\n- Catalog JSON/CSV generation passed with fail-on-unreviewed; review decisions unchanged. Existing generated web/mobile clients byte-match.\n- Independent [CI UI verification](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35055962490/job/104666174473) on head `f19fda5922fafe1e1290ec316a37c7c7a30da98b` passed all **216 suites / 2,055 tests**, lint, typecheck, Vite build and the initial-bundle budget. The actual merge checkout `1db6adcb9d1ccd76e21e957d7e56bcb7c158c03d` has the same source tree as that branch head. Job completed 2026-09-16 04:38:38 UTC.\n- Retained local limitations: first full web run failed three marketplace cases; unchanged isolated replay passed 10/10. One full rerun encountered different unchanged AdminUsers timeouts under heavy host load and was intentionally stopped (exit 143) after CI success. No timeout/assertion was weakened, no further full retry was made, and no local build is claimed. Full details remain in the evidence document.\n- Both owned Unix-socket PostgreSQL clusters stopped and independently verified stopped. No data deleted.\n\nExact commands, timestamps, commits, logs and limitations: `docs/payments/refund-execution-safety-2026-09-16.md`. Design: `docs/adr/0128-refund-execution-fence.md`.\n\n## Migration / rollout / risk\n\nNo schema migration, backfill or production data change. Existing migration chain and repeat-apply/empty rollback/reapply/used-history rollback-refusal checks passed in the disposable runtime harness. This is not a new full production-schema rehearsal.\n\nDrain old refund handlers before any future rollout: older binaries retain unsafe re-execution semantics. Prefer forward repair; binary rollback requires disabling affected refund commands while preserving reservations. Do not clear holds or retry with a new provider/key. SQL schema still permits some legacy transitions; this repair narrows application commands.\n\n## Explicit unfinished / blocked work\n\n- Automatic held-refund lookup/resolution, unknown-ID discovery, verified failure release, complete refund audit/intent projection and non-service financial allocations remain unfinished implementation, not credential-proven successes.\n- Staging hosting authentication and real merchant sandbox qualification remain unavailable/unverified. No provider flag enabled; no sandbox/staging/live payment, refund or payout request was made.\n- No native mobile change, refund/provider-specific browser/device E2E, screenshot, SRI issuance, legal/accounting/PCI certification, deployment or GitHub PR merge. General CI persona E2E reported success but was not inspected as refund qualification.\n- Keep all merchant, marketplace, legal/accounting and production activation gates in place. Overall payment-platform work remains incomplete.\n",
